## Topics Covered

### 1. Functional Testing Fundamentals
Learned:
- Functional testing validates application features
- Testing is based on business requirements
- Input → Process → Output validation
- Feature-by-feature verification

---

### 2. Types of Functional Testing

#### Smoke Testing
- Basic functionality verification
- Ensures build is stable for testing

#### Sanity Testing
- Quick validation after bug fixes or minor changes

#### Regression Testing
- Ensures existing features work after changes

#### Re-testing
- Confirms previously reported bugs are fixed

#### User Acceptance Testing (UAT)
- End-user validation against business needs

---

